provenance.prompt:
Use the supplied Nova Stitch gameplay sprite only as an identity and style reference. Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA sheet with exactly eight separate full-body Nova Stitch REVERSE layup poses in a four-column by two-row grid, row-major. All poses must be complete, in separate cells, at consistent scale. Right-facing on approach. Same human player, camera, palette, anatomy, outline and hair through the turn. No background, floor, court, hoop, shadow, glow, text, number, prop, teammate or opponent.

Nova is a young athletic fair-tan woman with long curly teal hair in a high ponytail, individual face, teal uniform with purple/black trim, black knee pads, teal-black shoes and wristbands. Preserve her exact identity, feminine athletic build, hair and outfit. No ball is drawn; basketball is separate gameplay art.

This is a reverse layup: Nova approaches the rim moving right, gathers, turns her shoulders/back away from the basket in flight, carries the invisible ball to the far side of her head and releases with the right hand on the reverse side of the rim. It must visibly differ from a normal forward layup. Eight unique connected full-body poses:
0 rightward approach, balanced stride;
1 gather hands near waist and prepare to plant;
2 TAKEOFF at tick2, leap with right knee rising;
3 airborne, rotate torso away so her shoulder/back turns toward viewer;
4 reverse-side peak, empty ball-miming hand reaches behind the crown with full ponytail unobstructed;
5 sole RELEASE at tick12, arm extends backward/high past her shoulder, palm open and already empty;
6 descend and unwind toward the court, arms counterbalance;
7 controlled landing with flexed knees and hands lowering.
No other release, no ball baked into any pose. Keep all limbs/hair/shoes complete and anatomically coherent.

Match the supplied 2D arcade sprite reference with crisp limited-palette 1990s pixel art and chunky dark outlines, not painterly, photoreal, 3D, glossy or anime. True transparent RGBA background, no alpha haze, matte or checkerboard. Return only the sprite sheet.
